===Glyph origin===
{{Han etyl}}
{{Han compound|來|夊|ls=psc|c1=p|c2=s|t2=footprint pointing down; to walk slowly}}; according to Xu Shen, its meaning is "wheat". {{zh-l|*來}} was the original character for “wheat”.

Several possible interpretations for the glyph:
* This character is a differentiation from {{zh-l|*來}}, which originally meant "wheat". It was then phonetically borrowed since the oracle bones to mean "to come". During the Warring States period, {{zh-l|*麥}} is attested and perhaps was coined specifically to mean "come". Eventually, since {{lang|zh|來}} lost its original meaning, this meaning shifted to {{lang|zh|麥}}.
* {{zh-l|*夊}} represents the ancient concept reported by ''{{w|Shuowen Jiezi}}'' that wheat came from the heavens (i.e., the Fertile Crescent).
* {{zh-l|*夊}} represents growth of the wheat plant.

===Etymology 1===
{{zh-forms|s=麦}}

Etymologically unrelated to {{och-l|來|to come}}. {{zh-ref|Schuessler (2007)}} suggests it is from {{inh|zh|sit-pro|*m‑rə(k)||buckwheat}} and cognate with {{cog|bo|བྲ་བོ||buckwheat}}; also compare {{cog|tbq-lob-pro|*g-ra²|t=buckwheat}}. STEDT compares {{och-l|麥|wheat}} to {{cog|tbq-pro|*bra||buckwheat}}  (provisional).

{{zh-ref|Starostin (2009)}}, on the other hand, compares this to {{cog|tuw-pro|*murgi||t=barley}}, {{cog|okm|밇|tr=milh|t=wheat}}, {{cog|ojp|麦|tr=mugi<sub>1</sub>|t=wheat; barley}}.

