===Etymology 1===
{{ja-kanjitab|yomi=k|もち}}

Cognate with {{m|ja|糯|tr=mochi||[[glutinous rice]]}}.<ref name="KDJ">{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}</ref><ref>{{R:Daijisen}}</ref><ref name="DJR"/>  The term ''mochi'' appears to have had a root meaning of {{m|en|[[sticky]], [[stickiness]], something sticky}},<ref>{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}, explanatory text at the bottom [https://web.archive.org/web/20210306175917/https://kotobank.jp/word/%E9%B3%A5%E9%BB%90%E3%83%BB%E9%BB%90-2068525#E7.B2.BE.E9.81.B8.E7.89.88.20.E6.97.A5.E6.9C.AC.E5.9B.BD.E8.AA.9E.E5.A4.A7.E8.BE.9E.E5.85.B8 here] in the {{m|ja||[語誌]}} section (in Japanese)</ref><ref>[http://gogen-allguide.com/mo/mochi.html {{m|ja||餅}} entry in Gogen-Allguide] (in Japanese)</ref> possibly from {{m|ja|持ち|tr=mochi||holding}}, the {{m|ja|連用形|tr=ren'yōkei||continuative or stem form}} of verb {{m|ja|持つ|tr=motsu||to [[hold]]}}.

The {{m|en|birdlime}} sense appears to have arisen from the use of a [[substance]] similar to [[pounded]] {{m|ja|糯|tr=mochi||[[glutinous rice]]}} to trap [[bird]]s and other small animals.  This substance was [[derived]] primarily from the [[bark]] of the {{m|ja|黐の木|tr=mochi no ki||{{taxlink|Ilex integra|species}}, the {{vern|mochi tree}}, a variety of [[holly]]}}.<ref name="KDJ"/><ref name="DJR"/><ref name="SMK5"/>

First appears in the ''{{w|Man'yōshū}}'' of 759 {{CE}}.<ref name="KDJ"/><ref>{{RQ:Manyoshu|13|3239}}, text available [https://web.archive.org/web/20220626150736/http://jti.lib.virginia.edu/japanese/manyoshu/Man13Yo.html#3239 here]</ref>

