===Etymology===
{{ja-kanjitab|くろ|y=k|alt=緇}}
{{wp|ja:}}
{{IPAfont|⟨kuro<sub>1</sub>⟩}} → {{IPAchar|/kuro/}}

From {{inh|ja|ojp|-}}, from {{inh|ja|jpx-pro|*kuro}}. See also {{ja-r|黒い|くろい}}.

Via root [[morpheme]] ''*kur'', cognates include:
* {{ja-r|涅|くり|[[black]] [[mud]] from the [[bed]] of a body of water}}.<ref name="KDJ">{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}</ref>
* {{ja-r|暗|くら|[[darkness]], [[deception]]}}, {{ja-r|蔵|くら|rom=-}}, {{ja-r|倉|くら|rom=-}}, {{ja-r|庫|くら|([[dark]]) [[storehouse]]}}, and {{ja-r|暗い|くらい|[[dark]]}}.
* classical verb {{ja-r|暮る|くる}}, modern {{ja-r|暮れる|くれる|to become [[dark]]; to [[near]] the [[end]] (of a [[day]], [[year]], [[life]], etc.)}}, {{ja-r|暗れる|くれる|rom=-}}, {{ja-r|眩れる|くれる|to become [[depressed]], to become [[dreary]] of [[mood]]}}, {{ja-r|暮れ|くれ|[[dusk]], [[nightfall]], [[sunset]]}}, and {{ja-r|呉|くれ|[[China]]|lit=[[land]] of the [[set]]ting [[sun]]}}.

Possibly also cognate with {{cog|ain|kur||shadow}} and {{cog|ko|구름||cloud}}; compare also {{cog|ja|-}} {{ja-r|雲|くも|[[cloud]]}}, {{cog|ko|-}} {{m|ko|[[검다|검—]]||black}}, and {{cog|ain|kunne||black; dark}}.

